On Tuesday 01 March 2011 14:13:34 .arpis. wrote:
> Sometimes I look up lujvo and get confused, because it seems like they have
> more than five places.  I usually assume I must be misunderstanding.
>
> ctufau
> f1 is a lesson by c1 for teaching audience c2 ideas/methods/lore c3 (du'u)
> about subject(s) c4 by method c5 (event).
>
> I don't see how I can be misunderstanding that.  What do you do if you want
> to fill the 6th place without filling the rest?  what if you want to refer
> to the 6th place in a sumti like {lo se ctufau}?  Does this have something
> to do with {xi}?  Is there some reference material I can look at?

"faxixa" or "sexixa". The FA or SE does not matter, e.g. "texivo" is the same 
as "ve". jbofi'e does not understand this; it thinks "texivo" is "te".

